        <div class="prose">
          <h2>Recovery across the full range of vehicles</h2>
          <p>"Vehicle recovery" is the umbrella under which our other, more specific pages sit. If you drive a standard car, our <a href="car-recovery-aberdeen.html">car recovery</a> page covers that in more detail; if you run a van for work, <a href="van-recovery-aberdeen.html">van recovery</a> is written specifically with tradespeople in mind. This page is for anyone who wants the broader picture — how we handle whatever's parked on your drive or stopped at the roadside, whatever type of vehicle it is.</p>
          <p>In practice that spans small hatchbacks and city cars, saloons and estates, 4x4s and SUVs, pickups, and vans and light commercial vehicles used for trade or business. Each has its own quirks when it comes to recovery, and we plan around them rather than treating every vehicle the same way.</p>

          <h2>Why vehicle type changes the recovery method</h2>
          <p>A low-slung sports car needs different ramp angles and loading care than a jacked-up 4x4. A long-wheelbase panel van has a different centre of gravity and turning circle to a small car, which affects how it's positioned on a flatbed. Ground clearance, overall weight, whether the vehicle is four-wheel drive, and how it's loaded internally all factor into whether we tow, winch onto a flatbed, or use wheel-lift equipment. Getting this right matters both for the safety of the recovery and for avoiding further damage to your vehicle.</p>

          <ul class="checklist">
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> Standard cars, estates and saloons.</li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> 4x4s, SUVs and pickups.</li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> Vans and light commercial vehicles.</li>
            <li><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg> Vehicles that aren't safe to drive due to a fault, damage, or being a non-runner.</li>
          </ul>

          <div class="callout">
            <p><strong>Tell us the details.</strong> When you call, let us know the vehicle type, roughly how big or heavy it is, and its condition. That's what lets us send the right recovery vehicle first time rather than having to reassess on arrival.</p>
          </div>

          <h2>Getting the right service for your situation</h2>
          <p>If your vehicle is a standard car and the problem is a straightforward mechanical fault, our <a href="breakdown-recovery-aberdeen.html">breakdown recovery</a> page is likely the closest match. If you're after recovery specifically for a van used for work, see <a href="van-recovery-aberdeen.html">van recovery</a>. This page exists for everything in between and everyone who just wants to know we can handle their particular vehicle before they pick up the phone.</p>
