        <div class="faq-list">
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>What types of vehicle can you recover?<span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></span></summary>
            <p>We recover cars, 4x4s, vans and other light commercial vehicles. Tell us the make, model and roughly how the vehicle is loaded (or if it's not loaded at all) when you call, so the right recovery vehicle and equipment can be sent.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Can you recover a 4x4 or larger vehicle?<span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></span></summary>
            <p>Yes. 4x4s and larger cars often need different handling than a standard hatchback because of their weight, ground clearance and sometimes four-wheel-drive systems, and we take that into account when planning the recovery.</p>
          </details>
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>Is there a weight limit?<span class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg></span></summary>
            <p>It depends on the vehicle being recovered. Tell us the vehicle type and approximate weight when you call, particularly for larger vans or heavily loaded vehicles, so we can confirm suitability before dispatch.</p>
          </details>
        </div>
